{
  "pdf_page": 508,
  "book_page": 478,
  "verified_by": "claude-opus-5.5",
  "verified_on": "2026-10-14",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 1,
      "root": "Teub, Tebh, Tebhos",
      "verdict": "unverified",
      "modern_form": "Mann's *tebh-, *tebhus (?) 'side' (not in Pokorny, Walde-Pokorny or Watkins/AHD)",
      "note": "The root is taken from Mann alone. IEC p.1371 (local IEC.txt line 18248-18250): 'tebh-, us (?) side. Cf. Supt. tueb-, toib- ... Per. tav, tū, s. fold, plait; Hitt. tapus, s. side. (The phonol. is obscure, as also that of Arm. kʿov side; Per. sū, suy, id.; Ir. taobh, id.; W tu, id.)'. Mann queries the root himself and says the phonology of the Armenian and Persian 'side' words is obscure. The comparison rests on Hittite tapuš 'side' and Old Irish tóeb / Irish taobh 'side'. Pokorny, Walde-Pokorny and Watkins have no such root. Mann's supplement page 1676 lies beyond the end of the local IEC OCR (it stops near p.1554). None of the four daughter nodes holds up: Pahlavi sōg and Armenian kʿov are phonologically impossible from *t-, Persian tū has no recorded etymology, and Arabic sūq is a Semitic word (Aramaic šūqā < Akkadian sūqu 'street'), not a borrowing from Persian sū.",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ *tebh- «پهلو» را تنها مان (Mann) آورده، آن هم با نشانهٔ پرسش. او خودش نوشته که پیوند واژه‌های فارسی و ارمنی با آن از نظر آوایی «مبهم» است. پوکورنی، والده-پوکورنی و واتکینز چنین ریشه‌ای ندارند. پایهٔ این مقایسه فقط هیتی tapuš و ایرلندی taobh «پهلو» است. شاخه‌های نمودار هم پذیرفتنی نیستند: «سو» از پهلوی sōg است و آغازه‌اش با t- هندواروپایی نمی‌خواند؛ ریشهٔ «تو» دانسته نیست؛ و «سوق» عربی واژه‌ای سامی است. پس خودِ ریشه نامطمئن است و شاخه‌هایش بیشتر رد می‌شوند.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/سو",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/تو",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/քով",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/سوق"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "IEC:1371", "status": "partial", "note": "IEC.txt line 18248-18250 (p.1371): 'tebh-, us (?) side ... Per. tav, tū, s. fold, plait; Hitt. tapus, s. side. (The phonol. is obscure, as also that of Arm. Kov side; Per. sü, suy, id.; Ir. taobh, id.)'. Mann has the root and the Persian/Armenian words, but queries the root and calls the Persian sū and Armenian kʿov comparisons phonologically obscure."},
        {"ref": "IEC:1676", "status": "not_found", "note": "Supplement page (the 'Supt. tueb-, toib-' cross-reference). The local IEC.txt ends at about p.1554 (858 leaves), so the supplement is not on disk."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "POK", "where": "POK_full/POK_01-03 grep 'tapus', 'taobh', 'tebh'", "stance": "silent", "note": "no root *tebh- 'side'; Hitt. tapuš and Ir. taobh are not cited"},
        {"src": "WLD", "where": "WLD_Bd1_pages.txt grep 'taobh', 'tapus'", "stance": "silent", "note": "no such root"},
        {"src": "AHD", "where": "AHD_watkins1985.txt grep 'tebh', 'taobh'", "stance": "silent", "note": "no root *tebh- 'side' in Watkins"}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Persian",
          "words": "tŭ",
          "verdict": "unverified",
          "derivation": "Persian tū / tōy (تو، توی، توه) 'fold, layer; inside', as in tū-be-tū 'fold upon fold' in the Tāherī Qazvīnī verse. The word exists in this sense. Its only link to *tebh- 'side' is Mann's list (IEC 1371: 'Per. tav, tū, s. fold, plait'), and Mann himself queries the root. An inherited *t- would survive in Persian, and *-bh- could in principle give -v- (tav), but no Middle Persian or Old Iranian ancestor of tū 'fold/inside' is attested. Wiktionary marks the etymology of the 'fold' and 'inside' senses as missing. No independent source either confirms or rejects the derivation.",
          "derivation_fa": "«تو» (توی، توه) به معنی «لا، چین» و «درون» در فارسی هست؛ در بیت طاهری قزوینی هم «تو به تو» به معنی لا به لا آمده است. تنها مان آن را در کنار ریشهٔ پرسش‌دار *tebh- «پهلو» آورده است. صورت فارسی میانه یا ایرانی باستانی برای این «تو» دیده نشده و ویکی‌واژه هم ریشه‌اش را نامعلوم می‌داند. پیوند آن با این ریشه نه تأیید می‌شود و نه رد؛ ادعای نورایی اثبات‌نشده است.",
          "sources": ["https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/تو"],
          "ref_check": [
            {"ref": "IEC:1371", "status": "partial", "note": "IEC.txt line 18250: 'Per. tav, tū, s. fold, plait', listed under 'tebh-, us (?) side' with the remark '(The phonol. is obscure ...)'"},
            {"ref": "IEC:1676", "status": "not_found", "note": "supplement page beyond the end of the local IEC OCR"},
            {"ref": "MON:1158", "status": "not_checked", "note": "Mo'in print page; vajehyab's تو entries returned only unrelated senses (e.g. 'لب تو رفتن') and could not be mapped to p.1158"}
          ],
          "consulted": [
            {"src": "HRN", "where": "HRN.txt grep 'Falte', entries tü/tö", "stance": "silent", "note": "Horn has no entry for tū 'Falte/innen'; only no. 455 np. cīn 'Falte' turns up"},
            {"src": "POK", "where": "POK_full grep 'tebh'", "stance": "silent", "note": "no root; the Persian tū is not cited anywhere"},
            {"src": "ARY", "where": "ARY_latin_index_pages.txt grep TAV / TU", "stance": "silent", "note": "no entry for تو 'fold' found"}
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "lang": "Pahlavi",
          "words": "sŭk, sôk",
          "verdict": "disputed",
          "derivation": "The word is real: Pahlavi sōg / sōk [swkʾ] 'side, direction' (MacKenzie: 'sōg [swk] side, direction; N sō(y)'; Nyberg: 'sōk [swk'] side; 4 ~ 4 gētē the four cardinal points ... NP sū, sūy'). Its derivation from IE *tebh- 'side' is impossible. Old Iranian *t- stays t- in Middle Persian and does not become s-, and *-bh- does not yield -k/-g. Horn (no. 748) states that no older form exists. Mann himself (IEC 1371) calls the Persian comparison phonologically obscure. The word has no accepted IE etymology.",
          "derivation_fa": "پهلوی sōg / sōk «سو، جهت» در مکنزی و نیبرگ آمده و نیبرگ آن را ریشهٔ «سو» و «سوی» فارسی می‌داند. ولی برگرداندنش به *tebh- از نظر آوایی ناشدنی است: t- ایرانی باستان در فارسی میانه s- نمی‌شود و bh- هم به k/g نمی‌رسد. هرن (شمارهٔ ۷۴۸) می‌گوید صورت کهن‌تری از این واژه در دست نیست. پس واژهٔ پهلوی درست است، ولی پیوندش با این ریشه را پژوهش امروزی نمی‌پذیرد.",
          "sources": ["https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/سو"],
          "ref_check": [
            {"ref": "HRN:165", "status": "contradicts", "note": "HRN.txt leaf 187 (p.165) no. 748: 'sū, sūi Richtung, Seite ... phlv. sūk Seite, Richtung. Eine ältere Form ist nicht vorhanden'. This supports the Pahlavi form but gives no IE root, so it does not support the arrow from *tebh-."},
            {"ref": "MON:1942", "status": "not_checked", "note": "Mo'in print page not mappable online; vajehyab سو returned only the 'manner' and Turkish 'water' senses"}
